meta {
  name: 01 List Tenants (via gRPC)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{bffUrl}}/api/v1/tenants?page=0&size=20
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  The BFF validates your JWT, then forwards the SAME token as gRPC
  metadata to accountservice (port 9095), which re-validates it and
  checks the account.read scope. A 200 here proves the whole zero-trust
  chain: browser token -> BFF resource server -> gRPC bearer forwarding
  -> accountservice JwtServerInterceptor -> R2DBC read.
}
